<title>USA: Hemagen says has FDA OK for arthritis test.</title>
<headline>Hemagen says has FDA OK for arthritis test.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hemagen Diagnostics Inc on Tuesday said it had received clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market a test for the detection of rheumatoid arthritis.</p>
<p>Carl Franzblau, president of Hemagen, said the rheumatoid factor test is in the increasingly popular enzyme immunoassay (ELISA) configuration which the company is using for many of the new assays it is developing.</p>
<p>Hemagen said it also markets a rheumatoid factor test in the hemagglutination format.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1610</p>
</text>
